  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656226",
      "title": "Using Services for Cross-Component Communication",
      "lectureOrder": 437,
      "videoOrder": 401,
      "sourceHash": "5ee66be43e4d5d90e5e665ca3f37df1b93641a7f753f65a2947d9120bde49bf1",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.429,
          "end": 6.27,
          "en": "-: We talked a lot about services in this module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.27,
          "end": 9.57,
          "en": "and I hope you saw how services can clean our app up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.57,
          "end": 12.15,
          "en": "make the code a bit leaner, more centralized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.15,
          "end": 13.463,
          "en": "easier to maintain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.463,
          "end": 17.13,
          "en": "You don't have to build these complex output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.13,
          "end": 20.04,
          "en": "input chains where you pass events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.04,
          "end": 24.42,
          "en": "and properties to get data from component A to component B.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.42,
          "end": 26.64,
          "en": "It's much leaner now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.64,
          "end": 30.72,
          "en": "Let me show you how much we actually saved.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.72,
          "end": 32.13,
          "en": "Let's say that if we click",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.13,
          "end": 35.91,
          "en": "on the button here in the account component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.91,
          "end": 39.72,
          "en": "for some reason we want to output something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.72,
          "end": 42,
          "en": "in the new account component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42,
          "end": 47,
          "en": "Normally without services, we would have to emit an event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.04,
          "end": 49.5,
          "en": "in the account component that something was clicked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.5,
          "end": 51.69,
          "en": "or something happened so that we changed the status,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.69,
          "end": 53.22,
          "en": "for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.22,
          "end": 55.11,
          "en": "We would have to catch the event here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.11,
          "end": 57.45,
          "en": "in app account as a site",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.45,
          "end": 60,
          "en": "or we can of course remove these events here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60,
          "end": 63.03,
          "en": "They don't, they aren't triggered anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.03,
          "end": 65.2,
          "en": "So we would have to catch these events here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.75,
          "end": 69.51,
          "en": "and then we would have to pass the new data down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.51,
          "end": 71.58,
          "en": "via property binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.58,
          "end": 75.45,
          "en": "QD component where we wanted to handle it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.45,
          "end": 76.98,
          "en": "Pretty complicated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.98,
          "end": 79.2,
          "en": "And building these chains of property and event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.2,
          "end": 82.5,
          "en": "binding is not the most convenient way of writing code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.5,
          "end": 84.78,
          "en": "It's so much easier with services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.78,
          "end": 87.15,
          "en": "Let's say in our account service here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.15,
          "end": 91.11,
          "en": "we want to provide some event which we can trigger",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.11,
          "end": 94.59,
          "en": "in one component and listen to in another.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.59,
          "end": 99.59,
          "en": "So we could simply add the status updated event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.69,
          "end": 101.65,
          "en": "which could be a new event emitter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.35,
          "end": 105.96000000000001,
          "en": "which we import from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.96000000000001,
          "end": 108.87,
          "en": "So make sure to add this import at the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.87,
          "end": 113.28,
          "en": "Which will pass on the new event, excuse me, the new status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.28,
          "end": 114.72,
          "en": "So a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.72,
          "end": 116.4,
          "en": "And yes, we could trigger it now here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.4,
          "end": 118.97999999999999,
          "en": "in the update status method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.97999999999999,
          "end": 122.04,
          "en": "But we can also, since we inject the account service here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.04,
          "end": 125.913,
          "en": "where we set the new status, call account service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.9,
          "end": 131.37,
          "en": "status updated and emit this with the new status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.37,
          "end": 134.34,
          "en": "So now I'm emitting an event I set up in the service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.34,
          "end": 137.85,
          "en": "And as a side note, later in the observable section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.85,
          "end": 142.85,
          "en": "you will learn about another construct you can use to submit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.95,
          "end": 147.15,
          "en": "or to emit events and subscribe to it instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.15,
          "end": 148.77,
          "en": "of using the event emitter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.77,
          "end": 150.93,
          "en": "But for now, that's absolutely fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.93,
          "end": 152.88,
          "en": "So here we are emitting an event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.88,
          "end": 156,
          "en": "Again, the event emitter lives in our service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156,
          "end": 159.09,
          "en": "And in a new account, I now want to listen to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.09,
          "end": 162,
          "en": "So here, let's say I want to throw an alert.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162,
          "end": 164.91,
          "en": "So I will do this in a constructor for now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.91,
          "end": 167.34,
          "en": "access my account service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.34,
          "end": 170.76,
          "en": "And now for the status updated event here, I will subscribe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.76,
          "end": 173.07,
          "en": "to it because event emitter in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.07,
          "end": 175.95,
          "en": "just kind of wraps an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.95,
          "end": 178.5,
          "en": "So here I could then receive the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.5,
          "end": 180.9,
          "en": "new status, which I know will be a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.9,
          "end": 182.85,
          "en": "And then I will simply throw an alert where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.85,
          "end": 184.383,
          "en": "I say, New status,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.91,
          "end": 187.533,
          "en": "status, something like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 188.52,
          "end": 190.86,
          "en": "So now I'm not building any chain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 190.86,
          "end": 193.38,
          "en": "of property and event binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 193.38,
          "end": 196.698,
          "en": "I do have cross component communication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 196.698,
          "end": 200.28,
          "en": "through a service with the event emitter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 200.28,
          "end": 202.653,
          "en": "And you can see this, if I click a button here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.85,
          "end": 205.47,
          "en": "they actually got opened on an hour window.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 205.47,
          "end": 208.23,
          "en": "But you see this alert was thrown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 208.23,
          "end": 210.36,
          "en": "with the new status unknown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 210.36,
          "end": 212.43,
          "en": "Same here, inactive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 212.43,
          "end": 213.66,
          "en": "Active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 213.66,
          "end": 216.57,
          "en": "So now we're communicating between components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 216.57,
          "end": 220.65,
          "en": "through a service, which really can save you a lot of time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 220.65,
          "end": 222.96,
          "en": "And with that, I hope you saw a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 222.96,
          "end": 225.57,
          "en": "of reasons why services can be very helpful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 225.57,
          "end": 228,
          "en": "and how you can use them to your advantages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 228,
          "end": 231.24,
          "en": "Make sure to use the right amount of instances.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 231.24,
          "end": 233.64,
          "en": "And if you inject services into services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 233.64,
          "end": 235.41,
          "en": "make sure to provide the service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 235.41,
          "end": 237.664,
          "en": "on the app module level and to add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 237.664,
          "end": 242.46,
          "en": "@injectable to disservice where you want to inject it in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 242.46,
          "end": 244.533,
          "en": "Let's move on to some assignments now.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
